<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's '97 LPG demand seen rising three percent.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's '97 LPG demand seen rising three percent.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's demand for liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) is expected to rise by three percent to 6.03 million tonnes in calendar 1997, the Trade, Industry and Energy Ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The estimated demand will break down into 4.03 million tonnes of propane gas, up 2.8 percent from this year, and two million tonnes of butane gas, up 3.5 percent, the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>LPG demand for city gas use is expected to fall 31.9 percent to 651,000 tonnes in 1997 as more and more homes are turning towards liquefied natural gas, it said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
